miniupnpc: stop the XML parser at the end of the buffer after '=' and after a namespace ':'

A router's reply that ends right after an attribute's '=' or right after a namespace ':' in an element name made parseatt()
and parseelt() read one byte past the buffer (CVE-2026-110655, CVE-2026-110656). The two checks are the functional hunks of
upstream commits 3cfb4fb78d5a and 64ef08a12aab, released after miniupnpc 2.3.3. The host runs this parser only with upnp on,
on the replies of the routers on the LAN (src/net/upnp_client.cpp).

--- a/src/minixml.c
+++ b/src/minixml.c
@@ -63,6 +63,9 @@
 				if(p->xml >= p->xmlend)
 					return -1;
 			}
+			/* p->xml points now to the character right after the '=' */
+			if(p->xml >= p->xmlend)
+				return -1;
 			while(IS_WHITE_SPACE(*p->xml))
 			{
 				p->xml++;
@@ -142,6 +145,8 @@
 				{
 					i = 0;
 					elementname = ++p->xml;
+					if (p->xml >= p->xmlend)
+						return;
 				}
 			}
 			if(i>0)
